===Etymology===
From {{af|en|lace|wing}}. Possibly a {{calque|nocap=1|en|mul|Neuroptera}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈleɪs.wɪŋ/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-lacewing.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of a number of [[gauzy]]-[[winged]] [[insect]]s of certain families within the order {{taxfmt|Neuroptera|order}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|title=Bulletin de la Société entomologique de France|volume=110|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=Uz0iAQAAMAAJ&q=%22thorny+lacewing%22%7C%22thorny+lacewings%22&dq=%22thorny+lacewing%22%7C%22thorny+lacewings%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=5xF6UvDHOIukkAXOx4CIBQ&redir_esc=y|page=128
|passage=We recently proposed a new genus of Thorny '''Lacewing''' (Insecta, Neuroptera, Rhachiberothidae) from the Eocene amber of France.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=David Grimaldi|title=Evolution of the Insects|page=356|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=Ql6Jl6wKb88C&pg=PA356&dq=%22thorny+lacewing%22%7C%22thorny+lacewings%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ES16Ur2lNceCkwXW-YGYCg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22thorny%20lacewing%22%7C%22thorny%20lacewings%22&f=false|passage=The family Rachiberothidae has been of considerable controversy and has been considered at different times during its history as a subfamily of Berothidae (Tjeder, 1959), or even of Mantispidae (Willmann, 1990b, 1004b). The "thorny '''lacewings'''" generally resemble other berothids except in the raptorial forelegs, which are convergent with those of the mantispids. While thorny '''lacewings''' are today confined to sub-Saharan Africa (U. Aspock and Mansell, 1994; U. Aspöck and H. Aspöck, 1997), they were clearly distributed throughout the world in the Cretaceous and perhaps into the Tertiary as well, disappearing from other regions apparently during the Eocene-Oligocene transition.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-10-21|title=Familial Clarification of Saucrosmylidae stat. nov. and New Saucrosmylids from Daohugou, China (Insecta, Neuroptera)|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0141048|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0141048|passage=As an extinct clade, many species of the saucrosmylids were erected just based on a single fore- or hindwing, and it should be realized that providing more stable characters is necessary when describing new '''lacewing''' taxa just based on an isolated hindwing.}}
# Any of various [[nymphalid]] butterflies of the genus {{taxlink|Cethosia|genus}} (order {{taxfmt|Lepidoptera|order}}).

